Package: zig
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: general-purpose programming language and toolchain
 Zig is a systems language with no hidden control flow, no hidden allocations
 and no preprocessor, and a toolchain that doubles as a drop-in C and C++
 cross-compiler: zig cc targets any supported triple from any host, bundling
 the libc headers it needs rather than requiring a sysroot per target.
 .
 This package carries the compiler and its standard library. LLVM is linked
 statically so the binary works on any of the archive's suites; the sources
 the compiler ships to build against live under /usr/lib/zig.
 .
 The compiler is bootstrapped from stage1/zig1.wasm, a prebuilt WebAssembly
 seed committed by upstream that is not reproducible from source. It does not
 influence the result: regenerating it with "zig build update-zig1" and
 rebuilding from the regenerated seed yields a byte-identical compiler.
